Redesign the EXISTING FlowAI landing page with a completely new visual theme.

Do NOT change the core product concept, content hierarchy, or primary CTA.

The brief remains:

FlowAI is an AI-powered workspace that helps growing teams organize work and automate repetitive tasks.

Target audience:
Growing businesses and modern teams.

Primary objective:
Encourage visitors to Book a Demo.

The current design feels too much like a typical “AI startup” website because of the strong purple/blue gradients, dark technology aesthetic, glowing elements and futuristic visual language.

I want to move away from that.

Create a new visual identity that feels like a PREMIUM MODERN BUSINESS PRODUCTIVITY PLATFORM rather than a futuristic AI product.

==================================================
1. NEW VISUAL PERSONALITY
==================================================

The new design should feel:

- Premium
- Calm
- Human
- Intelligent
- Sophisticated
- Modern
- Business-focused
- Trustworthy
- Editorial
- Product-led

Think:

Premium productivity software + modern editorial website + sophisticated SaaS.

The AI capability should still be present through the product experience and content, but the WEBSITE ITSELF should NOT scream “AI”.

Avoid:
- Neon gradients
- Cyberpunk
- Futuristic glowing interfaces
- Excessive purple
- Dark backgrounds everywhere
- Holographic effects
- Floating AI brains
- Excessive glassmorphism
- Excessive 3D
- Generic AI illustrations

The product should feel like something a serious growing company would actually buy.

==================================================
2. BACKGROUND STYLE
==================================================

Introduce a distinctive background system throughout the landing page.

Use soft:

“ambient gradient orbs”

also known as:

“blurred gradient blobs”
“soft gradient spheres”
“organic ambient shapes”

These should be large, subtle, blurred circular or organic shapes positioned behind sections.

IMPORTANT:

They should NOT look like obvious circles placed randomly.

They should feel atmospheric and integrated into the layout.

Use:
- Very soft blue
- Pale lavender
- Soft indigo
- Extremely subtle mint
- Off-white

Example:

A large soft blue orb behind the hero product.

A pale lavender orb partially behind the headline.

A subtle blue orb behind the AI automation section.

A very soft mint orb behind the final CTA.

Use high blur and low opacity.

The shapes can partially extend outside the section boundaries.

They should create depth without distracting from the content.

==================================================
3. COLOR SYSTEM
==================================================

Move away from the current strong AI-purple visual language.

Primary background:

#F8F9FC

Secondary background:

#F2F4F7

Cards:

#FFFFFF

Primary text:

#111827

Secondary text:

#667085

Muted text:

#98A2B3

Primary brand accent:

#4F46E5

Soft indigo:

#E9E7FF

Soft blue:

#EAF3FF

Very soft blue:

#F2F7FF

Success:

#20A88A

Border:

#E4E7EC

Use color sparingly.

The website should be approximately:

80% neutral
15% soft atmospheric color
5% strong accent

This should make the design feel mature and premium.

==================================================
4. TYPOGRAPHY
==================================================

Use Inter or Geist.

Typography should be one of the strongest design elements.

Large confident headlines.

Hero:

64–72px desktop.

Section headings:

44–56px.

Body:

17–19px.

Use dark navy/charcoal typography.

Do not use gradient text for every important heading.

Only use indigo emphasis on a few words where useful.

Example:

Work smarter.
Let AI handle the busywork.

Most text should remain dark.

==================================================
5. HERO
==================================================

Keep the two-column hero.

LEFT:

Small eyebrow:

AI-powered workspace for modern teams

Headline:

Work smarter.
Let AI handle the busywork.

Supporting copy:

FlowAI brings your team's projects, tasks and workflows into one intelligent workspace — while AI automates the repetitive work.

CTA:

Book a Demo →

Secondary:

See How It Works

Below:

No credit card required · 30-minute personalized demo

RIGHT:

Use a large horizontal 16:9 product demonstration/video area.

The product video should show FlowAI actually automating work.

The video should feel like a real SaaS product demonstration.

==================================================
6. HERO ATMOSPHERE
==================================================

Behind the hero product video, create:

One large blurred soft-blue gradient orb.

Behind the headline, create:

One very subtle pale-lavender organic gradient shape.

Near the bottom of the hero:

One extremely subtle blue/gray ambient shape.

The orbs should overlap visually with the whitespace but NEVER obscure text.

Use large scale.

For example:

Orb 1:
700–900px diameter
very soft blue
10–15% opacity
heavy blur

Orb 2:
500–700px
pale lavender
8–12% opacity
heavy blur

Orb 3:
400–600px
soft mint/blue
5–10% opacity
heavy blur

These should create an atmospheric background similar to premium modern SaaS/editorial websites.

